<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MapProbe</RootNamespace>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\ValveResourceFormat\ValveResourceFormat.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Renderer\Renderer.csproj" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.10" />
    <!-- The offscreen GL context the OpenGL side of the probe renders into, as in Tests.csproj. -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTK.Windowing.Desktop" Version="4.9.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The golden suite's backend scaffolding, compiled into this tool from where it already lives rather
    than copied.

    This is the deliberate coupling, and it is the point of the tool. The probe's whole claim is that a map
    fails (or renders) *the same way the gate would see it*, so it has to select the Vulkan driver by the
    same rule, refuse a hardware adapter by the same rule, trap direct OpenGL by the same rule and score an
    image against the same tolerances. Six copies of that logic drifting away from Tests/ would make every
    number the probe reports unattributable.

    A ProjectReference to Tests.csproj would be the tidier spelling and is not available: that project is a
    test host (NUnit, Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk, EnableNUnitRunner), so referencing it would drag the entire
    test suite and its runner into a developer tool, and Tests.csproj is not part of this solution. Linking
    the sources costs nothing at runtime, and none of these six files touches NUnit. They are already
    framework-neutral infrastructure that happens to live under Tests/.

    If a third consumer ever appears, extract these into a small class library that Tests.csproj and this
    both reference. With two, the link is cheaper than the project.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="..\..\Tests\Renderer\Golden\SoftwareVulkanIcd.cs" Link="Golden\SoftwareVulkanIcd.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\Tests\Renderer\Golden\ValidationGate.cs" Link="Golden\ValidationGate.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\Tests\Renderer\Golden\GLCallTrap.cs" Link="Golden\GLCallTrap.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\Tests\Renderer\Golden\VulkanGoldenDevice.cs" Link="Golden\VulkanGoldenDevice.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\Tests\Renderer\Golden\RhiDeviceCensus.cs" Link="Golden\RhiDeviceCensus.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\Tests\Renderer\Golden\ImageDiff.cs" Link="Golden\ImageDiff.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
